{%- comment -%}
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ARTICLE HERO HEADING
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Renders the hero heading of an article. The content comes from the "Hero heading" rich text metafield when set, and
falls back to the article title otherwise. Rich text metafields are wrapped in <p> tags, which are not valid inside a
heading, so paragraphs are unwrapped and paragraph breaks become line breaks.

Words italicised in the metafield are rendered with the italic heading font, through the "heading" snippet.

********************************************
Supported variables
********************************************

* article: the article to read the heading from
* style: the classes applied to the heading (for instance "h2 text-center isolate")
* indent: passed through to the "heading" snippet. Use "border_top" to draw the rule above the heading
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  capture hero_heading
    echo article.metafields.custom.hero_heading
  endcapture

  assign hero_heading = hero_heading | strip_newlines | replace: '</p><p>', '<br>' | replace: '<p>', '' | replace: '</p>', '' | strip

  if hero_heading == blank
    assign hero_heading = article.title
  endif

  render 'heading', content: hero_heading, html_tag: 'h1', style: style, highlight_effect: 'italic', indent: indent
-%}
